From 46ffcf395ae2f4a83f883805590a91449d3d4c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:23:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Guest networks: an Access Intranet pair of two guest networks
 joins only those two

- A network named on either side of ANY Access Intranet pair was treated as allowed onto the main
  network: it reached the router's pages, the main network's names and mDNS. Only a pair with the
  main network means that now.
- Two guest networks paired with each other forward to each other, both ways, IPv4 and IPv6; the
  router and the main network stay closed to both. A portal network gets main-network access only
  from a pair with the main network.
- Rule Status judges such a pair, and the Network page says what a pair does.
- reaper_fwsim.c also carries the walker's side of the OpenVPN Killswitch change of this rung.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
